Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Stamp build version as 7.3.33-CVE-2026-109618

NOTE: internal backport written for this rebuild environment - not an upstream
PHP artifact. The official upstream fix is 7.4-only.

Same intent as the PHP 7.4 series' 0001-version-marker.diff: make the rebuilt
binary self-identifying via `php --version`, and stop ./configure from
overwriting the patched main/php_version.h during build.

NOTE: internal backport written for this rebuild environment - not an upstream
PHP artifact. The official upstream fix is 7.4-only.

PHP 7.3's generated `configure` does not parse the version out of
`set $(echo <ver> | sed ...)` the way 7.4's does; it hard-codes PHP_MAJOR_VERSION
/ PHP_MINOR_VERSION / PHP_RELEASE_VERSION / PHP_EXTRA_VERSION. So the marker is
applied to PHP_EXTRA_VERSION there instead. PHP_VERSION_ID stays 70333.
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -3664,7 +3664,7 @@
 PHP_MAJOR_VERSION=7
 PHP_MINOR_VERSION=3
 PHP_RELEASE_VERSION=33
-PHP_EXTRA_VERSION=""
+PHP_EXTRA_VERSION="-CVE-2026-109618"
 PHP_VERSION="$PHP_MAJOR_VERSION.$PHP_MINOR_VERSION.$PHP_RELEASE_VERSION$PHP_EXTRA_VERSION"
 PHP_VERSION_ID=`expr $PHP_MAJOR_VERSION \* 10000 + $PHP_MINOR_VERSION \* 100 + $PHP_RELEASE_VERSION`
 
--- a/main/php_version.h
+++ b/main/php_version.h
@@ -3,6 +3,6 @@
 #define PHP_MAJOR_VERSION 7
 #define PHP_MINOR_VERSION 3
 #define PHP_RELEASE_VERSION 33
-#define PHP_EXTRA_VERSION ""
-#define PHP_VERSION "7.3.33"
+#define PHP_EXTRA_VERSION "-CVE-2026-109618"
+#define PHP_VERSION "7.3.33-CVE-2026-109618"
 #define PHP_VERSION_ID 70333
